  "body": "## Goal\nEstablish a screen-first, consumer-grounded visual coverage audit for the current Run Command vertical slice.\n\n## Scope\n- Inventory every target-build screen, focus state, overlay, transition, and relevant non-applicable family.\n- Map each surface to existing runtime consumers, approved assets, screen-level references, technical evidence, and bounded gaps.\n- Preserve the distinction between `SCREEN_DESIGN_REFERENCE`, runtime assets, Godot/procedural UI, and no-new-image-required surfaces.\n- Record five adversarial passes and handoff-ready, non-generative next actions.\n\n## Exclusions\n- No image generation, no visual asset approval/promotion, and no Godot gameplay or balance changes.\n- No inference of consumers for title, settings, save/load, or future progression screens.\n\n## Acceptance\n- P0/P1/P2 and not-applicable families are explicit.\n- The matrix links actual scene/node consumers and evidence.\n- Gaps are requirement/defer records, not automatic production work.\n- Repository and human-facing Notion summary are synchronized with readback.",
